================================================================================
llvm/llvm-project, MLIR bytecode format (layout of the StableHLO container)
================================================================================

The container `crates/mlmf-stablehlo` reads and writes (the four-byte magic,
the version varint, the NUL-terminated producer, sections with their
id-and-alignment byte, `0xCB` padding, and the prefix variable-width integer)
is specified in `mlir/docs/BytecodeFormat.md` of `llvm/llvm-project`, read at
commit `cced08fcc92db61044c0e32ef35444fa48246345` (blob
`27ce718fa3a62a2a730de3027b923a028f7fce91`). The LLVM project is under the
Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions; the text as that commit serves it
(`LICENSE.TXT`), sha256
`8d85c1057d742e597985c7d4e6320b015a9139385cff4cbae06ffc0ebe89afee`, is
`crates/mlmf-stablehlo/LICENSE-llvm.txt`. The section ids' names come from the
same document. No LLVM source is copied; the layout was also checked against
files written by MLIR itself.

`crates/mlmf-stablehlo/tests/fixtures/jax_export.mlirbc` is a StableHLO
portable artifact written by `jax.export` (JAX 0.12.0.1 / jaxlib 0.12.0.1,
Apache-2.0, producer `StableHLO_v1.18.0`) for a two-op function with invented
constants; `mlir_resource.mlirbc` is bytecode MLIR wrote (through jaxlib) for a
two-element `dense_resource` module; `rewritten_producer.mlirbc` is written by
this crate from the JAX file's sections and was parsed by MLIR to confirm it
(`verify_with_mlir.py`).
